-- cyclohexane, where the count depends on the temperature. Atoms: 0 to 5 the ring carbons in order, 6 to
-- 11 the axial hydrogen on each, 12 to 17 the equatorial hydrogen on each. The chair has the symmetry of
-- a three-fold rotation about its axis and three two-fold rotations through opposite bond midpoints, all
-- proper and all effectively instantaneous; the chair flip exchanges every axial hydrogen with the
-- equatorial hydrogen on its own carbon, is also proper, and has a barrier of 10.3 to 10.8 kcal/mol,
-- which puts its rate at about 10^5 per second at room temperature and at a few per second near 190 K.
--
-- the three-fold rotation, as one permutation: the carbons, the axial hydrogens and the equatorial
-- hydrogens cycled together
cyh-c3 : Nat → Nat
cyh-c3 = nat-comp (nat-cyc (cons 0 (cons 2 (cons 4 nil)))) (nat-comp (nat-cyc (cons 1 (cons 3 (cons 5 nil)))) (nat-comp (nat-cyc (cons 6 (cons 8 (cons 10 nil)))) (nat-comp (nat-cyc (cons 7 (cons 9 (cons 11 nil)))) (nat-comp (nat-cyc (cons 12 (cons 14 (cons 16 nil)))) (nat-cyc (cons 13 (cons 15 (cons 17 nil))))))))
